  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two dice are thrown independently. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;be the event that the number appeared on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st&#160;</mtext></msup></math> die is less than the number appeared on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mtext>nd&#160;</mtext></msup></math> die, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be the event that the number appeared on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st&#160;</mtext></msup></math> die is even and that on the second die is odd, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> be the event that the number appeared on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st&#160;</mtext></msup></math> die is odd and that on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mtext>nd&#160;</mtext></msup></math> is even. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pcocd",
      "text": "The number of favourable cases of the event&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LDybW",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are mutually exclusive",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RAyWe",
      "text": "The number of favourable cases of the events <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> respectively",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ec5bm",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;are independent",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>:&nbsp;No. on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st&#160;</mtext></msup></math>die <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo></math>&nbsp;No. on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mtext>nd&#160;</mtext></msup></math> die</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>:&nbsp;No. on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st&#160;</mtext></msup></math>&nbsp;die <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>even <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#38;</mo></math>&nbsp;No. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mtext>nd&#160;</mtext></msup></math>&nbsp;die <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> odd</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;No. on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st&#160;</mtext></msup></math> die <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>odd <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#38;</mo></math>&nbsp;No. on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mtext>nd&#160;</mtext></msup></math> die <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>even</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Now,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are not exclusive events</p><p>Now,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;are not independent</p>",
